{
  "abstract": "Formal statements and proofs, in Lean 4 with Mathlib, of parts of F. Najman, A. Trbović, \"Splitting of primes in number fields generated by points on some modular curves\" (Res. Number Theory 8 (2022)). For the 18 hyperelliptic models y² = f_N(x) of the paper (its explicit equations; their identification with the modular curves X₀(N) is not formalized), and quadratic fields ℚ(√D) generated by points with x ∈ ℚ and y ∉ ℚ: Theorem 2.2 (Table 2: primes that split, are unramified or not inert, and conditions on D), the square-residue conclusion of Theorem 2.8 (Table 3), Theorem 2.12 (infinitely many such fields in which a given prime ramifies, Table 4), and Theorem 2.13 with Table 7 in the corrected form of the authors' erratum (non-exceptional points), with the ring of integers, discriminant and residue rings of ℚ(√D). For Proposition 3.1 (complete splitting, in cubic fields K with E(K)_tors ≅ ℤ/2 × ℤ/14, of primes of multiplicative reduction): the local and algebraic steps, the passage from the torsion hypothesis to a point on the model of X₁(2,14), and the splitting conclusion under an explicit hypothesis replacing the step of the paper's proof that is not formalized. Also numerical checks against an exceptional point at level 26 and the printed Lemmas 2.6(b) and 2.9. 51 theorems and 1 definition, no sorry, only the axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.",
  "authors": [
